{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Six days you shall eat unleavened bread.</b> The verse brings it back, because the seventh day was set apart from the others. Another interpretation: <b>six days you shall eat unleavened bread</b> — this is not said to exclude the seventh day from the rest, but it refers to what precedes, and this is what it says: you shall turn in the morning and go to your tents, and all the six days remaining from there onward you shall eat unleavened bread." "<b>And on the seventh day.</b> It refers to the first day." "<b>Atzeret.</b> Restrain yourself on it from the things from which you restrained yourself on all the other days that passed."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:01.455314378Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}